# Area card

<h2 id="purpose">Purpose</h2>

An area card shows one room or area, such as “Kitchen”, as a single card. It can show the area’s picture or icon, short readings such as temperature and humidity, and an alert icon when something needs attention. Use it to give people a way into a room from a dashboard overview.

This page owns the Home Assistant area card (`type: area`). For how cards are built and grouped, see [Cards](cards.html) and [Dashboard composition](../home-assistant/dashboard-composition.html).

This page covers:

- Area card
  - `hui-area-card`

<h2 id="anatomy">Anatomy</h2>

From top to bottom:

- An optional picture, a camera view or the area’s icon. In every type except compact, the picture acts as a button when you set `image_tap_action` or `tap_action`.
- Alert icons on the picture, one for each active alert such as motion or moisture. The compact type has no picture: it shows a single alert badge on the tile icon instead.
- A tile with the area name, readings joined by a dot, and a round icon.
- Optional card features, below the tile or beside it.

If the area has no icon, Home Assistant draws a default texture icon.

